  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0201 database is used to store information about authors, books, customers, orders, and reviews. The authors table contains information about the authors of the books, including their first and last names, biography, birthday, nationality, and website. The books table contains information about the books, including their title, ISBN, genre, price, published date, author ID, and added date. The customers table contains information about the customers, including their first and last names, email, passcode, address, and phone number. The orders table contains information about the orders, including the order ID, customer ID, order date, total amount, status, and foreign key to the customers table. The review table contains information about the reviews, including the review ID, book ID, customer ID, rating, comment, and review date. The authors, books, and customers tables have primary keys, while the orders and review tables have primary keys and foreign keys to the corresponding tables. The foreign keys are used to enforce referential integrity, ensuring that the data in the child tables is consistent with the data in the parent tables.",
  "gold_question": "Background / Context\nThe project involves developing a comprehensive database system for an online bookstore, named `OnlineBookStore`. This system aims to efficiently manage books, authors, customers, orders, and reviews.\n\nObjectives\n- Design and implement a robust database to support core operations of an online bookstore.\n- Enable essential CRUD (Create, Read, Update, Delete) operations for managing data within the bookstore.\n- Support complex query handling to facilitate comprehensive data retrieval and manipulation.\n\nStakeholders & Users\n- End Users: Customers who interact with the website to browse and purchase books, and provide reviews.\n- Administrators: Internal users responsible for managing inventory, processing orders, and maintaining customer records.\n\nFunctional Descriptions\n1. Authors Management:\n   - Store author details such as name, biography, birth date, nationality, and website.\n   - Link books to respective authors.\n\n2. Books Management:\n   - Maintain details about each book, including title, ISBN, genre, price, published date, and associated author.\n   - Track book addition dates.\n\n3. Customers Management:\n   - Capture customer information including name, email, password, address, and phone number.\n   - Securely manage customer login credentials.\n\n4. Orders Processing:\n   - Record customer orders with order date, total amount, and status.\n   - Link orders to customers using unique identifiers.\n\n5. Reviews Handling:\n   - Allow customers to submit reviews with a rating and comments.\n   - Associate reviews with specific books and customers.\n\nNon-Functional Descriptions\n- Ensure secure data handling for customer information, particularly sensitive data like emails and passwords.\n- Optimize database performance for handling large datasets and complex queries.\n- Allow seamless scalability to accommodate an expanding inventory and growing customer base.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_codellama13b/0201.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0201\nCREATE TABLE `authors` (\n  `author_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `first_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `last_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `biography` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `birthday` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  `nationality` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `website` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`author_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `books` (\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `isbn` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `genre` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `published_date` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  `author_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `added_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`book_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `books_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`author_id`) REFERENCES `authors` (`author_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `customers` (\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `first_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `last_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL UNIQUE,\n  `passcode` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `address` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`customer_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `orders` (\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `order_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `total_amount` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`order_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `orders_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customers` (`customer_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `reviews` (\n  `review_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `rating` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `comment` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `review_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`review_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `reviews_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`book_id`) REFERENCES `books` (`book_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `reviews_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customers` (`customer_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
